      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Nutrition – Concept and Role in Life"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Nutrients are classified into macronutrients (carbohydrates, proteins, fats) and micronutrients (vitamins, minerals).",
        "Vitamins are divided into fat-soluble (A, D, E, K) and water-soluble (B-complex and C) categories.",
        "Proteins are essential for biological growth, tissue repair, and maintaining biological value.",
        "A balanced diet requires appropriate proportions of carbohydrates, proteins, fats, vitamins, minerals, water, and roughage.",
        "Malnutrition manifests as specific deficiency diseases resulting from inadequate intake of key vitamins and minerals."
      ],
